title Two faults whose errors cancel, and the four cures that each read worse
prompt the baton, and my own predecessor's recommend -- read the convergence census's denominator, since the two left unproven are a shared list and a remote-reading scan
rota lap 4476, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; law and boundary, walk the fence line and press each post. Single-Stranded gave the test that found the fault: check simplicity by trying to pull one part out. TAME_CORE root rules 1 and 4 -- bound everything, say why -- shaped the new reading's max and its comment.
think The recommend pointed at the population rather than the fraction, so the lap opened by running `sh tools/c/convergence_census.sh list` and reading both unproven candidates end to end rather than reasoning about their names.
think `tools/fixtures/d/dated_path_exclusions.sh` holds exactly one matching write and it is on line 93, inside a `#` comment explaining why the repointer is the sharper half. The census counted a sentence about writing as a write. Its own header names that family twice -- prose about idempotence is a claim, a scan counting a mention as a use -- and both its PROOF columns learned to read past a leading `#` at `20260908.190452`. The WRITE column never did.
think `tools/fixtures/u/upstream_shape_scan.sh:150` is a real `cat "$f.t" > "$f"`, and it runs inside a `git filter-branch --tree-filter` string over `*.txt` in a `mktemp -d` pen. A pen write has nothing to converge, which is exactly what the `*_control.sh` exclusion is a proxy for; the file is named `_scan.sh`, so the name-based proxy misses it. Named rather than cured -- the honest key is whether the write lands in a pen, and reading that needs to see inside a quoted filter-branch argument.
think Then the pull-one-part-out test, and this is the finding. Stripping comment lines alone takes the population 12 -> 9, and the three that leave include `reds_ledger_headline_write.sh` and `index_shelf_repair.sh` -- both real writers, both run on every commit by `tools/hooks/pre-commit`, and `reds_ledger_headline_write.sh` is the one tool `convergence_tree_prove_witness.rish` proves converges on every lap of every ship. They were candidates ONLY through their comments, because their real targets are `$LEDGER` (line 114) and `$shelf` (line 218) and neither name is in the target filter's list.
think So the write reading carries two faults and their errors cancel: it admits the right files for the wrong reason. That is why four laps refining this one pattern never converged -- each moved one strand and measured the pair. All four candidate cures were RUN on this tree before anything was written: comments dropped alone 12 -> 9 and loses both; variable targets admitted unless a named pen 12 -> 49, the fourth wrong denominator returning, because this tree writes scratch under a hundred local names; a bounded 3-hop resolution of the target variable through its own file's assignments 12 -> 14, admitting `reds_fold.sh` (a real writer the card mandates) beside three pen writers ($SCRATCH, the seed projector, the roster runner's own receipt); a widened room list goes stale the day a room is born.
think Every cure read worse than the fault, so the lap printed the reading instead of acting on it. `admitted_on_comment_only` counts the candidates whose admission rests on a comment, `list` prints each path, and no existing number moves -- the census reads 12/10/2 before and after. A ratchet that publishes a count and names no member is a finding no ship can act on, which is REDS %671, booked by a peer eleven hours earlier one guard over.
think The Rishi half of the recommend went the other way from the header's projection. The header predicted a widening blindness from the 2,450-to-939 language ratio; read one site at a time, all 13 `write-file` sites in `tools/` target a pen (`tools/.build/readme_metrics_block.md`), untracked custody (`.git/ssh_config_jail`, `gpg.sh`, `.wireguard/`), or a fixture roundtrip. The one real Rishi tree-writer is `tools/g/geode_libraries.rish:22`, whose target is an unquoted `docs-geode/libraries/README.md` inside a `run ["sh" "-c" ...]` string, and the tree prover already reads it `converges` on every lap.
obs The structural reason is worth more than the count: this tree's Rishi tools render into `tools/.build/` and hand the pen to a shell splice, so the census reading the splices IS reading the Rishi tools' tracked writes, one layer down. `readme_metrics.rish` is the exemplar -- it writes the block to `tools/.build/` and calls `readme_metrics_splice.sh README.md block_path`. A reading whose population looks shell-shaped is reading a composition rather than a language.
obs The control's elder leg is the one that makes this provable rather than plausible: `elder_could_not_tell_prose_from_a_write` runs the elder write predicate over the same two plants and asserts it calls them identical. Without it the four new legs pass for any reason at all, which is how four of this census's five wrong denominators read green.
obs Reds first held: all 15 OPEN rows read as custody gates, shape decisions awaiting Keaton's word, or peer-owned, so no row was agent-closable and the constructive lane was open.
obs The pin took the real cost. `construction/ITINERARY.md` stood 26 bytes under its 40,960 at HEAD, so the account had to land within its elder's 867 bytes; it took nine passes of condensing to reach 995 and then 40,957 total. The four cure numbers stay on the card because they are the finding; the full table lives in the census header, which is the record a card only advertises.
