status GREEN -- convergence_census_witness (27 legs, 0 fail), convergence_census_control standalone, tame_style_check, shell_dialect_witness, pin_bound_touch_witness all green; cold pass 217 guards 213 green with both reds the custody-gated `sow_allow_reach` and the roster's own summary of it; hot pass run before the commit
recommend keep-going -- the pen question is the next post on this fence: `upstream_shape_scan.sh` writes inside a `filter-branch --tree-filter` string in a `mktemp -d` pen, and the `*_control.sh` exclusion is a name where the honest key is the write's destination. Reading that needs to see inside a quoted argument, which is the same capability the spoken-ASCII meter already walks.
